  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fixes\n\n- Async methods now wait for their callbacks (#409, closes #397). For a method returning Task, Task<T>, ValueTask or ValueTask<T>, a callback returns a Task, and that task used to be dropped: an exception in an async callback was never observed, and the call completed before the callback had. Callbacks still start when the method is called, in the order they were added. The task the method returns now completes after the arranged result and every callback that hadn't finished, and fails with the first failure. Callbacks that complete synchronously leave the arranged task unchanged.\n\n  Behaviour change: a test whose async callback fails now sees that failure when it awaits the call.\n\nMaintenance\n\n- AsyncCallbacks is a new public type in Imposter.Abstractions, for generated code only. It is hidden from IntelliSense.",
